    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1101">

                <pb facs="1221" n="1211" xml:id="pg1211"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 EW/12–644: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-12-06">December 6,
                        1944</date>.<lb/>[Received December 6—6:29 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4659. Press for December 6 publish[ed] prominently Lublin account dated December
                    3 of hanging of five Hitlerites sentenced for crimes committed in Majdanek death
                    camp.</p>
                <p>Execution was witnessed by over 20,000 persons who according to story, hurled
                    imprecations at Hitlerites, such as “that is what they deserve”. Despatch adds
                    that execution was greeted by stormy approval.</p>
                <p>Sent to Department as 4659, repeated to London as 285 for Schoenfeld.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harriman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
